====================================================================================
STAGE 3 PRE-LOAD GRAPH IDENTITY CHECK
====================================================================================

  Refuses to invoke the Stage 3 Joern runner unless the graph on disk is
  byte-for-byte the graph EVERY record of account describes -- the frontend log
  when this checkout's frontend wrote one, the provisioning record beside the
  graph itself, and always the identity declared by
  harness/ENVIRONMENT.md section 7. Records that disagree
  are fatal and none is preferred for matching. It also adjudicates the graph's
  METHOD COUNT against AAP 0.9.2's floor of 853,420, because
  identity and completeness are different facts: a truncated graph persisted
  once has a consistent identity in every record that describes it. The runner
  MEASURES and PRINTS its input's size and digest, and harness/lib/joern-scan.sc
  calls importCpg and then counts, so without this comparison a mismatch or a
  truncation would reach the engine.

  Any fatal finding here exits 77. The callers that refuse on it are
  harness/lib/run-joern-gated.sh, which has no branch reaching the runner after
  a non-zero gate, and the run of record, which publishes this report to
  harness/artifacts/logs/joern-preflight.log immediately before the Stage 3
  load. harness/bin/run-joern.sh does NOT read it: it prints its input's
  identity without comparing it, and it is REFERENCE under AAP 0.6.1, so closing
  that inside the runner is a provisioning change whose patch is recorded in
  oss-scan-results/run-record.md. A direct invocation of that runner is
  therefore not bound by this status.

